        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "jemc:cc-ts-2026-01-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 3 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Wholesale Power Cost Adjustment factor. Schedule P-22 increases or decreases every bill by a per-kWh factor the Cooperative computes each month from its estimated purchased-power costs and sales, and publishes no factor. The JSON-LD defines the adjustment as a per-kWh PriceDefinition with no Price, so a modeled bill is high or low by the month's factor times its kWh. (2) Temporary or seasonal service. The schedule applies to any customer whose service is temporary or seasonal in nature. The EligibilityRule carries non-residential customer kind, as the Cooperative lists the schedule among its commercial rates; the condition is in its description only. (3) Terms of Payment. The sheet adds a late fee and disconnection charges under the Service Rules and Regulations and makes all charges subject to applicable taxes. Neither is priced on the sheet and neither is carried.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-18T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
